completely inaccessible to the user.

To Reproduce:
- Search for a game with long release names (e.g., "Hogwarts Legacy").
- Click on the game to open the Download/Search results menu.
- Observe that for long titles, the download icon on the far right is cut off and cannot be reached.

Environment:
OS - Windows
Browser - Chrome
Version - 1.3.0

I was able to temporarily fix this in the browser console by forcing the title elements to wrap using this code that was given to me by AI:
// 1. Find the elements that are causing the width explosion
const longTitles = document.querySelectorAll('.text-sm.font-bold, .truncate');

longTitles.forEach(title => {
    // 2. Force the text to wrap or truncate properly
    title.style.whiteSpace = 'normal'; 
    title.style.wordBreak = 'break-word';
    title.style.display = 'block';
});

// 3. Ensure the parent doesn't grow wider than the modal
const rows = document.querySelectorAll('.relative.flex');
rows.forEach(row => {
    row.style.maxWidth = '100%';
    row.style.overflow = 'hidden';
});

console.log("Layout tightened! Check if the download buttons are visible [now.");

