When adding games from IGDB or creating new games, the client was potentially sending fields that should never be included in POST requests: `id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `isReleased`, and `inCollection`. These are either database-generated or future state fields.

## Changes

Added client-side filtering to `client/src/lib/api.ts`:

- **New utility function** `filterGameDataForPost()` that strips restricted fields using object destructuring
- **Applied to POST endpoints**: `gameAPI.create()` and `discoveryAPI.addToCollection()`

```typescript
const filterGameDataForPost = (gameData: any): InsertGame => {
  const { id, createdAt, updatedAt, isReleased, inCollection, ...validData } = gameData;
  return validData as InsertGame;
};

// Usage
create: async (gameData: InsertGame): Promise<Game> => {
  const filteredData = filterGameDataForPost(gameData);
  const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/games`, {
    method: "POST",
    body: JSON.stringify(filteredData),
    // ...
  });
}
```

This prevents validation errors and ensures only valid fields reach the server, regardless of what the client-side game object contains.

